          "fact": "L2",
          "source": "cor-one-dimensional-change-of-variables-with-absolute-derivative",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $a<b$, let $\\varphi$ be $C^1$ and injective on a neighborhood of $[a,b]$, and suppose $\\varphi'(x)\\ne0$ there. If $f$ is continuous on an interval containing $\\varphi([a,b])$, then\n$$\\int_{\\min\\{\\varphi(a),\\varphi(b)\\}}^{\\max\\{\\varphi(a),\\varphi(b)\\}}f(y)\\,dy=\\int_a^b f(\\varphi(x))|\\varphi'(x)|\\,dx.$$\nThus the absolute derivative is the correct factor for the unoriented image interval.",
