          "fact": "L5",
          "source": "lem-em-spherical-harmonic-basis-and-addition",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$), with the exact meaning of [[def-countable-choice]]. Let $P_l$ denote the real vector space of homogeneous polynomials of degree $l$ on $\\mathbb R^3$ ([[def-homogeneous-polynomial-and-homogeneous-ideal]], [[def-monomials-multidegree-and-total-degree]]), $H_l=\\ker(\\Delta:P_l\\to P_{l-2})$ with $P_k=\\{0\\}$ for $k<0$, and let spherical harmonics of degree $l$ be the restrictions of $H_l$ to $S^2$, with unnormalised surface measure $d\\Omega$ of total mass $4\\pi$ ([[def-surface-integral-on-a-compact-c-one-hypersurface]], [[lem-euclidean-chart-measure-agrees-with-polar-surface-measure]]). Then $P_l=H_l\\oplus|x|^2P_{l-2}$, $\\dim H_l=2l+1$, harmonics of distinct degree are orthogonal in $L^2(S^2,d\\Omega)$, and the union over $l$ of the spaces of spherical harmonics admits a complete orthonormal basis of $L^2(S^2,d\\Omega)$ ([[def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis]]). For any real orthonormal basis $Y_{lm}$, $m=1,\\dots,2l+1$, of degree-$l$ harmonics the addition theorem holds:\n\n$$\\sum_{m=1}^{2l+1}Y_{lm}(n)Y_{lm}(n')=\\frac{2l+1}{4\\pi}P_l(n\\cdot n'),$$\n\nwhere $P_l$ is the Legendre polynomial of the convergent zonal kernel lemma ([[lem-em-convergent-legendre-kernel]]). The Laplacian is the Euclidean one ([[def-laplacian-of-a-c2-function]]). This supplies the harmonic decomposition, orthogonality, completeness and exact addition kernel; it does not assert higher boundary regularity. The purely polynomial decomposition and finite dimension identities use no Choice; the surface/$L^2$/completeness claims retain the stated Countable Choice.",
