          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^n$, $n\\ge2$, be a bounded $C^1$ domain or have the specified finite piecewise $C^1$ presentation. For real $u\\in C^2(\\overline\\Omega)$ and $v\\in C^1(\\overline\\Omega)$, $$\\int_\\Omega(v\\Delta u+Du\\cdot Dv)\\,dx=\\int_{\\partial\\Omega}v\\partial_\\nu u\\,dS.$$ In the piecewise case the right side is the sum over faces, counted once off E. All integrals are finite.",
