          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $\\Omega\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be a **bounded smooth graph domain**: a nonempty bounded open set such that for every $x\\in\\partial\\Omega$ there are an open neighbourhood $W\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ of $x$, a rigid motion $R(p)=Qp+b$, an open ball $B\\subseteq\\mathbb R^2$ and a function $h\\in C^\\infty(B;\\mathbb R)$ such that, after shrinking $W$ so that $R(W)\\subseteq B\\times\\mathbb R$,\n\n$$R(\\Omega\\cap W)=R(W)\\cap\\{(y,s)\\in B\\times\\mathbb R:s<h(y)\\},$$\n\nwhich is the $C^\\infty$ case of the bounded $C^k$ graph domain of [[def-bounded-c-k-domain-and-boundary-charts]]. Let $V\\subseteq\\mathbb R^3$ be an open set with $\\overline\\Omega\\subseteq V$. Then there exists a real-linear operator $E_\\Omega$, determined only by $\\Omega$, a finite smooth atlas and fixed cutoffs, such that for every open interval $J\\subseteq\\mathbb R$ ([[def-interval]]) and every function $u:\\Omega\\times J\\to\\mathbb R$ that is of class $C^\\infty$ on the open set $\\Omega\\times J$ and whose every mixed derivative $D^\\alpha\\partial_\\tau^j u:\\Omega\\times J\\to\\mathbb R$ has a continuous extension to $\\overline\\Omega\\times J$ ([[def-ck-and-multi-index-notation-in-several-variables]], [[def-directional-and-partial-derivatives]]), the function $E_\\Omega u$ is of class $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times J$, satisfies $E_\\Omega u(x,\\tau)=u(x,\\tau)$ for all $(x,\\tau)\\in\\overline\\Omega\\times J$ and\n\n$$D^\\alpha\\partial_\\tau^j(E_\\Omega u)\\big|_{\\overline\\Omega\\times J}=\\text{the continuous extension of }D^\\alpha\\partial_\\tau^j u$$\n\nfor all multi-indices $\\alpha$ and all $j\\ge0$, and is spatially supported in one fixed compact subset of $V$, in the sense that there is a compact $K_\\Omega\\subseteq V$ with $E_\\Omega u(x,\\tau)=0$ for all $x\\notin K_\\Omega$, $\\tau\\in J$. For every compact $K\\subseteq J$, every integer $m\\ge0$ and every $j\\ge0$,\n\n$$\\sup_{\\tau\\in K}\\|\\partial_\\tau^j E_\\Omega u(\\cdot,\\tau)\\|_{C^m(\\mathbb R^3)}\\le C_m\\sup_{\\tau\\in K}\\|\\partial_\\tau^j u(\\cdot,\\tau)\\|_{C^m(\\overline\\Omega)},$$\n\nwhere $\\|w\\|_{C^m(\\overline\\Omega)}:=\\sum_{|\\alpha|\\le m}\\sup_{x\\in\\overline\\Omega}|D^\\alpha w(x)|$ and $\\|W\\|_{C^m(\\mathbb R^3)}:=\\sum_{|\\alpha|\\le m}\\sup_{x\\in\\mathbb R^3}|D^\\alpha W(x)|$, and the constant $C_m$ depends only on $m$, $\\Omega$, the atlas and cutoffs. The extension commutes with every time derivative: $\\partial_\\tau^j(E_\\Omega u)=E_\\Omega(\\partial_\\tau^j u)$ for all $j\\ge0$. No bound uniform over an unbounded $J$ is asserted. Vector-valued inputs of finite dimension are extended componentwise. The construction adds no choice principle: the finite atlas is selected from the cover of all admissible smooth chart patches, finite cutoffs come from the published choice-free compact cutoff lemma, and the infinite coefficient sequence is defined by the explicit formula below. The consuming elliptic or Sobolev argument retains whatever choice principles its own suppliers declare.",
