          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $Q=\\prod_{j=1}^3(0,L_j)$ with $L_j>0$ and let $\\varepsilon,\\mu>0$ be constants. Define the reflection boundary class by extending $E_1$ evenly across the $x_1$-walls and oddly across the $x_2,x_3$-walls, and cyclically for $E_2,E_3$; extend $B_1$ oddly across $x_1$ and evenly across $x_2,x_3$, cyclically for $B_2,B_3$. Work on the rectangular torus $\\prod_j\\mathbb R/(2L_j\\mathbb Z)$ in the real $L^2$ fields with these parities and distributional $\\operatorname{div}E=\\operatorname{div}B=0$. For smooth fields the parity class gives $n\\times E=0$ and $n\\cdot B=0$ on $\\partial Q$. Then: (i) the finite separated Fourier modes are dense in this class, and the class is complete for the $L^2$ pairing ([[lem-l-two-with-the-integral-pairing-is-a-hilbert-space]], [[def-orthonormal-family-complete-orthonormal-system-and-hilbert-basis]]); (ii) for every initial datum in the class there is a unique $C(\\mathbb R;L^2)$ weak solution of $\\partial_tE=(\\varepsilon\\mu)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}B$, $\\partial_tB=-\\operatorname{curl}E$ in the same class ([[def-distributional-derivative]]); (iii) the energy $\\tfrac12\\int_Q(\\varepsilon|E|^2+|B|^2/\\mu)\\,dx$ is constant along the solution. This is an explicit weak PEC model; it supplies neither trace regularity for arbitrary $H(\\operatorname{curl})$ fields nor completeness in lossy, open or non-rectangular guides.",
