        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "thm-em-waveguide-spectral-completeness",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice ([[def-axiom-of-choice]]). Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^3$ be a bounded $C^\\infty$ domain in the local graph sense of [[def-bounded-c-k-domain-and-boundary-charts]], with outward Euclidean unit normal field $\\nu$ on $\\partial\\Omega$. Restate the class conventions of [[lem-em-smooth-pec-cavity-spectral-closure]]: $L^2:=L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^3)$ is the real Hilbert space of square integrable vector fields with the inner product $\\langle u,v\\rangle=\\int_\\Omega u\\cdot v\\,dx$ induced by the Euclidean inner product of [[def-euclidean-inner-product]], and\n$$H(\\operatorname{curl})=\\{u\\in L^2:\\operatorname{curl}u\\in L^2\\},\\qquad H(\\operatorname{div})=\\{u\\in L^2:\\operatorname{div}u\\in L^2\\}$$\nare the graph spaces with norms $\\|u\\|^2_{H(\\operatorname{curl})}=\\|u\\|_2^2+\\|\\operatorname{curl}u\\|_2^2$ and $\\|u\\|^2_{H(\\operatorname{div})}=\\|u\\|_2^2+\\|\\operatorname{div}u\\|_2^2$, the curl and divergence being taken in the distributional sense; $X$ is the graph-norm closure in $H(\\operatorname{curl})\\cap H(\\operatorname{div})$ of the fields that are smooth on a neighbourhood of $\\overline\\Omega$ and satisfy $\\nu\\times u=0$ pointwise on $\\partial\\Omega$; and $V=\\{u\\in X:\\operatorname{div}u=0\\}$, $H=\\overline V^{\\,L^2}$. This is the explicit weak perfect-electric-conductor class of that item, not an identification with every maximal tangential-trace realisation.\n\nThen:\n\n(a) **Smooth PEC cavity.** The curl form $(u,v)\\mapsto\\int_\\Omega\\operatorname{curl}u\\cdot\\operatorname{curl}v$ on $V$ has a complete orthonormal $L^2$ eigenbasis $\\{u_j\\}$ with nonnegative eigenvalues $\\lambda_j$ of finite multiplicity, with $\\lambda_j\\to\\infty$ whenever $H$ is infinite dimensional and with the finite-dimensional zero eigenspace retained. Each eigenfield $u_j\\in V$ satisfies $\\int_\\Omega\\operatorname{curl}u_j\\cdot\\operatorname{curl}v=\\lambda_j\\int_\\Omega u_j\\cdot v$ for every $v\\in X$; the eigen-equation $\\operatorname{curl}\\operatorname{curl}u_j=\\lambda_ju_j$ holds distributionally together with the PEC trace; and $u_j$ has a $C^\\infty$ representative on $\\overline\\Omega$ for which $\\operatorname{div}u_j=0$, $\\nu\\times u_j=0$ and $\\partial_\\nu u_{j,n}+(\\operatorname{div}\\nu)u_{j,n}=0$ hold classically on $\\partial\\Omega$, where $u_{j,n}=u_j\\cdot\\nu$ and $\\nu$ is extended constant along collar normal lines. For every explicitly chosen positive mathematical speed $v_{\\mathrm{wave}}>0$ and every pair of data $q_0\\in V$, $q_1\\in H$, the associated second-order wave has coefficients solving $a_j''+v_{\\mathrm{wave}}^2\\lambda_ja_j=0$ with $a_j(0)=\\langle q_0,u_j\\rangle$ and $a_j'(0)=\\langle q_1,u_j\\rangle$, in the modal class of that item: its displacement lies in $C(\\mathbb R;V)$ and its velocity in $C(\\mathbb R;H)$, finite modal sums converge in $C(K;V)$ and $C(K;H)$ on every compact time interval $K$, and the finitely many $\\lambda_j=0$ modes are $a_j(t)=a_j(0)+ta_j'(0)$. The speed is a positive abstract mathematical parameter and has no physical dependency. The scalar auxiliary Dirichlet resolvent used inside the recorded cavity argument has, for every $q\\in L^2(\\Omega)$, a unique solution $\\varphi\\in H_0^1(\\Omega)\\cap H^2(\\Omega)$ of $(1-\\Delta)\\varphi=q$, with smooth zero-boundary approximants converging in $H^2$ and whose gradients converge in the PEC graph norm, by [[lem-em-dirichlet-resolvent-h-two-and-smooth-test-density]]. For smooth $q$ this solution is smooth on the closure by the same smooth-boundary bootstrap; no classical regularity for a general $L^2$ datum is asserted. Smooth unshifted scalar boundary problems have the classical upgrade of [[thm-em-elliptic-boundary-existence]] with $\\varepsilon=I$.\n\n(b) **Rectangular reflection-parity class.** Let $Q=\\prod_{j=1}^3(0,L_j)$ with $L_j>0$ and let $\\varepsilon,\\mu>0$ be constants. In the reflection boundary class of [[lem-em-rectangular-pec-energy-completeness]] (real $L^2$ fields on the torus $\\prod_j\\mathbb R/(2L_j\\mathbb Z)$ whose components carry the parities of that item and whose distributional divergences vanish), the finite separated Fourier modes are dense at every time, and every initial datum of the class has a unique $C(\\mathbb R;L^2)$ weak solution of $\\partial_tE=(\\varepsilon\\mu)^{-1}\\operatorname{curl}B$, $\\partial_tB=-\\operatorname{curl}E$ in the class, along which $\\tfrac12\\int_Q(\\varepsilon|E|^2+|B|^2/\\mu)\\,dx$ is constant.\n\nNo completeness is asserted in lossy, open-ended or non-smooth classes, and the constant-Ohmic and open-longitudinal branches are homed separately as physical items on the guide page; they are not mathematical premises or dependencies of this statement.",
