      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "step-1-1",
          "claim": "The sphere trace and its harmonic extension. On $S^2$ the outward unit normal is $\\nu(n)=n$, so the normal derivative of $x_3$ is $\\partial_nx_3=\\nabla x_3\\cdot n=e_3\\cdot n=n_3$; thus $x_3$ is harmonic on $\\mathbb R^3$ by [F1] and has boundary trace $f(n)=n_3$ on $S^2$. The function $f$ is continuous, hence in $L^2(S^2)$ with coefficients $f_{lm}$, so the ball boundary branch [F7] applies: the series $\\sum_{l,m}r^lf_{lm}Y_{lm}(n)$ is the unique harmonic function on $B_1$ with $L^2$ boundary limit $f$ and continuous extension to $\\overline B_1$. Since $x_3$ is such a harmonic function, the branch identifies the extension as $u(x)=x_3$; in particular $f=n_3$ is an admissible ball-boundary datum, not an excluded class.",
