          "quote": "(a) [Root and emission-time Jacobian] For every $(x,t)\\in\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$ (equivalently $x\\ne z(t)$) there is exactly one $s=s(x,t)<t$ with $t-s=|x-z(s)|/c$. The map $s:\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma\\to\\mathbb R$ is of class $C^3$, and with $R:=x-z(s)$, $r:=|R|$, $n:=R/r$, $\\beta:=z'(s)/c$ and $\\kappa:=1-n\\cdot\\beta$ ([[def-euclidean-inner-product]]) one has $$\\partial_ts(x,t)=\\kappa^{-1},\\qquad \\nabla_xs(x,t)=-\\frac{n}{c\\,\\kappa},\\qquad \\kappa\\in[1-v_*/c,\\,1+v_*/c],$$ so $\\kappa\\ge 1-v_*/c>0$ uniformly on $\\Omega\\setminus\\Gamma$. Moreover, for the fixed $x$ and near the root, the function $s'\\mapsto s'+|x-z(s')|/c$ is differentiable at $s'=s$ with derivative $\\kappa(x,t)$: this emission-time Jacobian $1-n\\cdot\\beta$ is the denominator produced by the delta substitution of clause (b).",
