          "source": "thm-em-wave-cauchy-kirchhoff",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ($\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$), used through the cited published suppliers ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $c>0$, $t_0\\in\\mathbb R$, $T>t_0$, let $a,b\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3)$ and let $h\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_0,T])$ in the extension sense that $h$ is the restriction of a $C^\\infty$ function on $\\mathbb R^3\\times J$ for some open interval $J\\supset[t_0,T]$ ([[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]). Write $W:=c^{-2}\\partial_t^2-\\Delta$, so that $c^2W=\\Box_c$ is the wave operator of speed $c$ ([[def-laplacian-of-a-c2-function]], [[def-wave-equation-cauchy-data-and-wave-speed]]). For $\\varphi\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3)$ and $s\\ge0$ let $H_\\varphi(x,s):=s\\,M_{cs}\\varphi(x)$, where $M_r\\varphi(x)=\\frac{1}{4\\pi}\\int_{S^2}\\varphi(x+rn)\\,d\\Omega(n)$ is the spherical mean of [[lem-em-spherical-mean-wave-identity]]. Define, with $s=t-t_0$, $$u(x,t):=\\partial_sH_a(x,s)+H_b(x,s)+c^2\\int_{t_0}^{t}H_{h(\\cdot,v)}(x,t-v)\\,dv,\\qquad (x,t)\\in\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_0,T],$$ where $h(\\cdot,v)$ denotes the map $x\\mapsto h(x,v)$ and $\\partial_sH_a$ is the partial derivative of $H_a$ in its second argument, evaluated at $s=t-t_0$. Then:\n\n(a) $u$ is of class $C^\\infty$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_0,T]$ in the extension sense, $Wu=h$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times(t_0,T)$ (indeed on the open neighbourhood of the closed time interval on which the extension of $h$ is defined), $u(\\cdot,t_0)=a$ and $\\partial_tu(\\cdot,t_0)=b$.\n\n(b) Uniqueness: every $v\\in C^2(\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_0,T])$ in the extension sense with $Wv=h$ on $\\mathbb R^3\\times(t_0,T)$, $v(\\cdot,t_0)=a$ and $\\partial_tv(\\cdot,t_0)=b$ equals $u$.\n\n(c) Domain of dependence: let $\\tilde a,\\tilde b\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3)$, $\\tilde h\\in C^\\infty(\\mathbb R^3\\times[t_0,T])$ and let $\\tilde u$ be the corresponding solution. If $\\tilde a=a$ and $\\tilde b=b$ on the closed ball $\\overline B_{c(t_*-t_0)}(x_*)$ and $\